    "body": "## Description\n\nCreate `docs/getting-started.md` — a step-by-step guide for brand new contributors explaining how to go from zero to their first merged pull request.\n\n## Steps to Complete\n\n1. Create `docs/getting-started.md`.\n2. Write a guide covering:\n   - Creating a GitHub account (if needed)\n   - Forking the repository\n   - Cloning it locally\n   - Creating a branch\n   - Making a small change\n   - Committing and pushing\n   - Opening a pull request\n3. Include screenshots or command examples where helpful.\n4. Link to it from `CONTRIBUTING.md`.\n5. Commit with `docs: add getting started guide`.\n6. Open a pull request.\n\n## Learning Outcomes\n\n- Deep understanding of the fork-and-pull-request workflow.\n- Technical writing for beginners.\n\n## Helpful Resources\n\n- [GitHub Docs: Contributing to projects](https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/quickstart/contributing-to-projects)\n- [First Contributions](https://github.com/firstcontributions/first-contributions)\n",
